// Title: Potential Provisioning Registry Key Abuse For Binary Proxy Execution
// Sigma ID: 2a4b3e61-9d22-4e4a-b60f-6e8f0cde6f25
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel
// Date: 2023-08-08 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects potential abuse of the provisioning registry key for indirect command execution through
//   "Provlaunch.exe".
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Provlaunch/
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1674399582162153472
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_provlaunch_provisioning_command.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Provisioning\\Commands\\"
